            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>While nuclear medicine is essentially an imaging specialty, it often provides functional information which may not be obtained in any other way. This review considers how best such information can be presented and how physicians can become more familiar with nuclear medicine techniques.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
